---
import evidence from "../../../docs/benchmarks/evidence/native-roadmap-fresh-uat-2026-10-18.json";
const seconds = Number(evidence.full43_engine_seconds);
if (evidence.full43_calls !== 43 || !Number.isFinite(seconds) || seconds <= 0 ||
    !evidence.all_members_reopened || evidence.performance_claim) {
  throw new Error("Benchmark summary requires complete, non-comparative Full43 evidence");
}
---
<p><strong>ShardLoom: {seconds.toFixed(3)} seconds</strong> of engine execution across the {evidence.full43_calls}-query
  ClickBench workload, one execution per query, recorded on
  October 18, 2026. The source Parquet data had already been loaded into Vortex;
  loading was separate, and operating-system cache state was not controlled.</p>
<p>Complete values and schemas were verified. This development-build observation is
  not an official ClickBench cold or warm score, a comparative speedup, or a
  measurement of the published package. The evidence retains loading and storage details.</p>
<details>
  <summary>Recorded configuration</summary>
  <dl>
    <dt>System and interface</dt><dd>ShardLoom, SQL through the CLI.</dd>
    <dt>Hardware and operating system</dt><dd>macOS 27 ARM64; 10 logical CPUs and 16 GiB physical memory.</dd>
    <dt>Resources</dt><dd>24 GiB query memory allocation and maximum parallelism 12. The allocation is not a whole-process memory ceiling.</dd>
    <dt>Source and stored data</dt><dd>99,997,497 rows imported from Parquet into Vortex before the query pass; 15,713,610,513 bytes of stored Vortex data.</dd>
    <dt>Build</dt><dd>Development revision {evidence.source_commit.slice(0, 12)}, with the Vortex 0.85.0 provider used by that recorded build.</dd>
    <dt>Measurement</dt><dd>One execution of each of 43 queries. Engine execution time; loading, separate validation, and report generation excluded. Operating-system cache uncontrolled.</dd>
  </dl>
</details>
<p>Source <a href={`https://github.com/depsilon/shardloom/tree/${evidence.source_commit}`}><code>{evidence.source_commit.slice(0, 12)}</code></a> ·
